Operator directive 2026-08-07 ("tackle #1" -- adopt the Duck/TAAF leaderboard
lesson of object-level, not raw-grid, perception), amending the 2026-08-03
one-slot ruling. The mechanism already existed and was already A/B'd
positive: the pre-registered 2026-08-01 held-out change-fidelity A/B
(results/outer_loop_arc_object_perception_heldout_ab_change_fidelity_20260801.json)
measured this exact flag SIGNIFICANT on its primary metric (mean delta
+0.072084, sign-test p=0.0192 over 19/20 discordant games, min reachable
p=3.81e-06, gemma-4-31B, 13171.65s real GPU wall time, AA control
byte-identical, clean on live adversarial re-check) but shipped with the
flag deliberately left off -- recorded explicitly as "moving it is a
separate operator decision." This commit is that decision.

_object_perception_on(): os.environ.get("CARNOT_ARC_OBJECT_PERCEPTION") ==
"1" (default off) -> os.environ.get("CARNOT_ARC_OBJECT_PERCEPTION", "1") !=
"0" (default on, opt out with =0). Every induce_prompt call now appends the
connected-component OBJECT STRUCTURE table (translation-invariant
object_hash, containment, adjacency) unless explicitly disabled.

Tests updated in lockstep, not just left to bit-rot: the crash-guard test
that asserted "unset -> no object block" now asserts "unset -> object block
present, no crash", with a new symmetric guard for the opt-out path and the
byte-identity check flipped to assert "1" == unset rather than "0" == unset.
32/32 pass across test_object_perception_induction.py and
test_object_perception_ab_stats.py (the latter's own A/B-comparison test
updated to set both arms explicitly rather than relying on unset-means-off).

NOT done here (forward work, per the spec entry): per-transition
BEFORE/AFTER object diffs, translation-invariant tracking across those
diffs, and HUD-strip rejection inside the object table specifically --
today's table covers only the initial grid + win-precursor/opening-board
frame. These are the genuine remaining Duck/TAAF-adoption work, distinct
from flipping an already-evidenced flag.

Artifact-freshness: 6 artifacts drifted on arc_executable_world_model.py.
5 had zero references to induce_prompt/CARNOT_ARC_OBJECT_PERCEPTION in
their generating scripts (grep-verified, genuinely unrelated). One
(outer_loop_arc_generator_concurrency_fix_20260727.json) DOES call
induce_prompt directly, inside a helper that self-calibrates the transition
count k via the server's real tokenizer until a target TOKEN COUNT is
reached -- so the harness converges on the same target prompt SIZE
regardless of what content (object block or not) fills those tokens; its
acceptance gates are about n_ctx/concurrency/mutation-testing, not prompt
content. artifact-freshness-lint: OK.

